The Wayland protocols the self-blurred backdrop captures the screen with
(capture.c), and the source of the generated glue one directory up:

  ext-image-copy-capture-v1.xml     wayland-protocols 1.48, staging
  ext-image-capture-source-v1.xml   wayland-protocols 1.48, staging
  ext-foreign-toplevel-list-v1.xml  wayland-protocols 1.48, staging (only
                                    because ext-image-capture-source names
                                    its handle interface)
  wlr-screencopy-unstable-v1.xml    wlr-protocols (unstable-2022-09-05)

Regenerate after replacing an XML (wayland-scanner 1.24.0 made these; the
flake's `wayland-glue` check compares them):

  for x in *.xml; do
    n=${x%.xml}
    wayland-scanner client-header $x ../$n-client-protocol.h
    wayland-scanner private-code $x ../$n-protocol.c
  done
